  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — skewness — is not present in the verbal report. The individual does not consider the distribution of outcomes or the probability of unfavorable results. Instead, the individual focuses only on the absence of risk (risk-free gain), which is a different justification. The decision reason requires evaluating skewness and preferring a more right-skewed lottery, but neither lottery is right-skewed; in fact, Lottery B is left-skewed. Since the individual does not mention skewness or any feature related to it, and instead relies on risk-free gain, the decision reason was not used. Therefore, the individual did not apply the skewness-based decision reason to make the choice.",
